{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tianchi-fetch/factory-sandbox/pulls/13","id":4519287839,"node_id":"PR_kwDOUYQzws8AAAABDV7cHw","html_url":"https://github.com/tianchi-fetch/factory-sandbox/pull/13","diff_url":"https://github.com/tianchi-fetch/factory-sandbox/pull/13.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/tianchi-fetch/factory-sandbox/pull/13.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tianchi-fetch/factory-sandbox/issues/13","number":13,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"#6: tally total is wrong","user":{"login":"github-actions[bot]","id":41898282,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDE4OTgyODI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/15368?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/github-actions","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Closes #6\n\n## Problem\n\nFinance's export uses currency-formatted amounts (`$1,234.56`, `$12.00`). `float()` rejects the `$` and thousands `,`, so `tally` exits 1 instead of producing a total, and finance's total (1246.56) never gets reproduced.\n\n## Fix\n\n`cell_values()` in `src/tally/__init__.py` strips a leading `$` from the cell, then strips `,` before calling `float()` — but only when the comma forms a well-formed thousands grouping (1-3 leading digits, then groups of exactly 3, and no comma in the fractional part). A comma that doesn't fit that shape (a European decimal comma like `1.234,56`, or a stray `1,3` / `12,34,5` / `,234`) still raises `TallyError` naming the row, instead of silently summing to a wrong total.\n\nThe error message for genuinely unparseable values still reports the original, unstripped cell text, and the group key (used when `--group-by` names the same column as `--column`) is still built from the raw, unmodified text — only the value being summed is cleaned.\n\nParenthesized negatives and non-USD symbols are intentionally not handled — not evidenced by the report.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `uv run pytest -q` — 39 passed (37 pre-existing + 2 new: currency parsing, malformed-comma rejection).\n- Reproduced the reporter's exact scenario:\n  ```\n  vendor,amount\n  Acme,\"$1,234.56\"\n  Bolt,$12.00\n  Crane,\n  ```\n  `uv run python -m tally finance.csv --column amount` now prints `1246.56`, matching finance's figure.\n- Reproduced the review's counterexamples (`1.234,56`, `1,3`, `12,34,5`, `,234`) and confirmed each still exits 1 with a row-numbered error, and that well-formed grouped values (`1,234,567.89`, `-1,234.56`, plain `1234.56`) still parse correctly.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n","created_at":"2026-09-13T15:01:26Z","updated_at":"2026-09-13T15:13:09Z","closed_at":"2026-09-13T15:13:09Z","merged_at":"2026-09-13T15:13:09Z","merge_commit_sha":"4139b4ef99a2d51300221f50065581dd44a3127e","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":false,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tianchi-fetch/factory-sandbox/pulls/13/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tianchi-fetch/factory-sandbox/pulls/13/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tianchi-fetch/factory-sandbox/